   149	**Page.** The panel sits at the second bell on day 201 (`manuscript/chapter-51.md:127–157`). The frame is warm, the panel finds Iron, and entry requires Brom's signature before Halcenvane's registrar within fourteen days (`manuscript/chapter-52.md:125–145`). Brom folds the finding, neither signs nor refuses, and chooses the three boxes (`manuscript/chapter-52.md:153–171`). The finding and guidance slip end beside the unopened, uncracked envelope (`manuscript/chapter-53.md:117–123`).
   150	
   151	**Governing text.** The ratified date is day 201 at the second bell (`STATE_LEDGER.md:1022`). B6's binding end state is “advancement to Iron found and never signed; Copper formal forever” (`BOOK_MAP.md:91–96`). The day-45 letter must remain sealed on Brom's table (`STATE_LEDGER.md:1028`; `packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:34`). M9 does not require either paper to move.
   152	
   153	**Ruling.** Exact. The panel outcome, non-signature, non-refusal, and envelope all pass. The new guidance slip is a compatible mechanism that dramatizes why a true finding still costs Brom his association; it changes neither rank nor inheritance.
