   141	He knew what lay in that pause as well as he knew his own Log. It was the true argument. She had just told a seat, with perfect accuracy, that its instrument had failed to read him, and she knew why it had failed, and what was appended to the reading, and how long it had been so, and whose hands had signed for it. She could have dated the thing to within a renewal of Greyvane's charter. It would have taken her nine minutes, and she had the nine minutes.
