     5	He looked at the two figures after the room had emptied. He had written a great many pairs of times in that book since the fortieth day, and he could not remember looking at a pair before, for it was not his place to notice how long a thing had taken. It was his place to see that anybody who wanted to know could find out. He blotted them.
