    99	It was a form. He had drawn it from the district seat's stationery press some weeks ago, on the day after the eleventh sitting, and had carried it blank ever since: *Request for relief from rotation*, a single leaf with five ruled heads. He had never filled one in. In all his service he had gone where he was sent and stayed until he was fetched.
