   140	
   141	Then Lira came round the corner at something that was nearly a run, and stopped herself, and walked, and Brom came after her at his own pace. He looked just as he had looked going in, with his coat buttoned, except that there were two red bars across his forearms where the cuffs had ridden up, darker than the wool press had left them.
