    35	So they walked beside the cart, all of them, and on the worst pitches Brom and Seln put their backs to the tailboard, and Cael put his right shoulder there, low, where it did not have to lift. Karis carried a wedge of ash from the crossroads fire, and each time the gelding stopped she had it under the wheel before the cart could run back a hand's breadth. She did it forty times before noon, and her face was grey with it, and she would not give the wedge to anyone.
    36	
    37	"They're mine," she said, when Brom put out his hand. "I can't carry them. I can at least stop them rolling."
    38	
    39	It was on that hill that the list grew short.
