   157	There had been a ferry there once. Cael saw the posts first, two on each bank, black and leaning, and a flat boat lying on the near shingle with its bottom stove in and grass growing through it. It had been kept for when the water was up and a loaded wagon could not ford. A board lay face down in the grass by the nearer post, and he turned it over with his foot. The paint had gone, but the letters had been cut before they were painted, and he could read them. *Foot. Horse. Cart, loaded.* The registry's seal was at the head of it.
