    89	Seln opened his mouth, and shut it.
    90	
    91	Cael watched him. He had seen that face across a counter for two years and had never once seen it lose, and it was losing now, to three people at a fire; and he thought that somewhere under the mildness the man was more pleased than he had been since a birthday.
    92	
    93	"Mm," said Seln.
    94	
