   963	- (a) **The room** is Karis's reading room at the top of the library (M5's page), not "a stone room two floors below the library" (packet). Owner flag 1.
   964	- (b) The case is gone from its shelf on day 88's morning (M5 put it back on day 81); the packet's "down for days" is not used.
   965	- (c) The three routes are habit, not instruction (Seln: "Come the way you always come").
   966	- (d) The debt is paid the same night as the cache, with the circle present (they shared the seal).
   967	- (e) The clean door is found from the code and the house's old enrollment book, borrowed from Bracken "for a citation".
   968	- (f) Vastin is brought to Ostrand by his own yearly river inspection (B5 ch50's station inspection), and summoned by an unsigned note quoting his Norhold note.
   969	- (g) The Vastin window adds the junior at the door, told "Continue observation" — spoken, not written; he files nothing and writes nothing.
   970	- (h) Cutaway: Vastin ~1,850 words (packet ~2k). No other cutaway (M6 ~94% Cael).
   971	
   972	## New canon minted (flag where marked)
   973	
   974	- **The cache (flag):** forty pairs (a copied station Kindling record with the keeper's frame reading and margin, and a clipped *Order of reclassification at evaluation* — *Per corrective classification at Kindling evaluation: enter …. Margin reading not to be entered. Observe nine weeks following entry.* — with a back slip *Observed nine weeks. Nothing to report.*); twenty-three field reports stamped *Read against file. Enter at file.* (some with *Continue observation*; one *Noted, and I do not like it.*); nineteen printed memoranda, *Memorandum to keepers of stations and to clerks of entry. Corrective classification at Kindling evaluation.*, three sentences, reissued about every ten years, seventy-one signatures, none twice; **the leaf** (ink, no seal, grey-brown paper): *Of the advisory corrections function. The function is appended to the reading and is not the reading. It does not alter what the reading shows. It advises what is to be entered, and the entry is made as advised. It is to be maintained, and its maintenance is the office's charge.*
   975	- **The father's letter and the clerk's four lines (flag; texts mine, ch35).**
