   105	They left him at first light on the Fourth-day.
   106	
   107	It was the last day of the academic year. Cael had known it when he woke, as one knows a date that has been set against one's name for a long time. Somewhere behind him, six switchbacks up from a river, a bell would ring that evening and the house would close its books; and at some hour between, on a north road short of a toll-bar, a stout fair man would unlock a windowless building. He did not know the hour, for Withrow's sheet had given only the day, and he found that he kept looking at the sun.
