editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:29:- **Lowmarch, day 60:** fourteen slips. Seln reads the board and takes the well: "I keep waiting for someone to ask for my report." **Brom at the plank's end:** "What does the board pay a man with no Path at all." / "Same as anyone… What'd he do?" He writes it on an old slip and keeps it against his skin, the second time in his life (Rooke was the first). Pike: "Held a dog with a shoulder and a river, that one." **The mail** sorted aloud. Hesk's letter (protected), and the grandmother he did not know about. The log. **The saying** at the book, the sheet rewritten by hand: twelfth. "Teague's still eleven up. He'll speak to you when you've cost him something."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:25:- **Day 91:** marked at the plank in front of eleven witnesses. The mail: **Ephram** and **Vell** (texts protected). **The void road (day 92):** the registry's printed sheet against the ground (seven dashed roads ending in white; this is the third); Karis's carter's map with three blank circles; "Their map has no roads. His has no quiet ground. Between them you get the country." Ephram's letter read at the wash at noon (Bracken told the registry "the Line and nothing past it"; Lira: "Good."). Vell's read at noon on the 94th, aloud, to Lira ("She puts the thing that decides it last." / "So does Ephram.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:27:- **Days 94–95, six on the Fallow road** (Oryn on the mule's down-slope side; the registry sheet goes back into the box at the east gate; past Thornwater's fork the printed sheet is white). **The rise:** he looks at the dark place where an Arbiter would be. Lira's hand up: "It's like the air got thick." Brom: "Like a door closing behind me." Oryn's hands half-raised and silent. Karis: "My Arbiter's gone." Seln: "Back up. Ten paces. Tell me when it comes back." Five *backs* at one stride. The stone. **Cael felt nothing, either way, and says nothing**, for two reasons: he doesn't know what it means, and nobody asked. The log at the stone (protected). Camp on the road, no fire. The floor takes the last light like water, and Oryn holds her hands over the line until it's gone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:25:- **The birthday (day 102):** Lira instigates one-armed, pays one-handed, and has been practising the pouch for a week without saying so. Brom acquires three kinds ("Three."). Six places in the common room. Oryn at the table "like a woman who has sat at a great many tables and stayed at none of them." **The line written** (protected). "A stop. Good. Write it down before it changes." **Pike's Fallow copy** by carter; "Six went in. Six came out." beside Gault's last note. Hesk's package does not come, and the absence sits at the table unremarked. Seln: "He's counted her… So has the broker." The apples argument, which Karis loses on the merits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:32:- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The winter fence** given over ("Ours."). Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "Spring." **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
