editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:116:- **The Power Log** (in Hesk's satchel; about a third of its leaves left) and **the observation notebook**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:153:- **Vell** in Ardenmere. One letter in, one out. "The session still stands" stays unexplained.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:17:- **Where/when:** the switchback shelf above an unnamed valley, the first camp beyond the Registry Line. Book 7 dates everything *past the Line*: Book 6's "sixth day" from Ostrand is Book 7's **second day past the Line**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:19:- **Cael:** eighteen (turned on the page in B6 Ch14). **Nine confirmed fragments + the Tide-adjacent anomaly** (session nine, B2), uncounted, under the standing words "Still open. Still real. Patience." No injury open (the Crown-yard forearm bruise is a week from gone; the eleven-minute bill was paid on the road east). The Power Log is in Hesk's satchel, about a third of its leaves left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:21:- **Companions:** Lira, Wind, Iron R1 formal (Silver bracket declined at full price). Brom, Iron Skin, Copper formal for good, continental Copper champion. Karis, Ember, ranking forfeited, three boxes made into a field archive. Seln, Shadow, Bronze, left the Compact in form, carrying the locked case (the machine's own maintenance records). All uninjured. Lira and Brom have read the log. Karis sees demonstrations, not the log. Seln knows the mechanism since B6 Ch15.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:23:- **Objects:** a cart, a horse, three boxes and Seln's case under one canvas (B6 Ch24; see conflict C1). Two letters, to Hesk and to Vell, written at the shelf and held for the first westbound courier. Daeva's reply already went west from the ford. The registry's printed continental sheet and the Ternhall straightedge are in Karis's middle box.
