   309	The clerk had met such slips before, though not often. There was one of them on this file already. It was older than any other paper in it, older than the first leaf, and it had given the subject a designation that two careful officers had since tried to trace and could not. That one sat at the head of the file, and this one had come to its foot.
   310	
   311	Such a slip did not explain itself. It said what was to be entered, and a clerk did not ask it for its authority, any more than one asks a pen. The slip advised, and the entry was made as advised.
   312	
   313	The clerk dipped the pen and wrote a fifth line under the four, in the same ink.
   314	
   315	*Status: active non-compliance, observation priority escalated.*
   316	
   317	It was blotted. The clerk looked at it for as long as it takes ink to lose its shine. It did not agree with the four above it, for a matter could not well be moot and also active; but that was not the clerk's to reconcile.
   318	
   319	The file was not tied, and it was not carried down to the press. A file with that line at its foot was not finished, whatever else was written on it. It went back onto a different shelf, among others of its kind, with its spine outward, where it could be reached.
   320	
   321	Nobody had signed for the line. No office was named on it.
   322	
   323	---
   324	
   325	"They will not close it," said Seln.
   326	
   327	He had not yet lain down. He was sitting by the fire with his coat round him and his cup in his hands, and Lira and Karis were awake as well, since nobody had found the way to sleep on the first night of a place. Brom had come back from the lip to warm his hands. So all five of them were there, and the pine was burning with its high clear flame.
   328	
   329	"The file," said Seln. "I have been thinking of it, since I shall not be let stand a watch. A subject who withdraws is closed. A subject who withdraws and then goes where no district runs is a different matter, and there is a line for that; I have copied it on to other people's files, in my time." He turned the cup. "It says *non-compliance*, which is an odd word for a man who has complied with everything. Then it says that the priority of observation is escalated. It is a form. It means that somebody is told to look harder."
