+# Book 6 close -> Book 7 plan reconciliation: F rerun
+
+> Independent plan audit: Sol (Codex), 2026-10-11  
+> Authority: surviving edition Book 6 prose, chapters 48-60, read in full; then the AFTER MOVEMENT 7-9 coordinator rulings and CLOSED notes. Where the visible prose and a coordinator ruling differ, the coordinator ruling is identified explicitly. No author end-state was used by itself.
+
+## Result
+
+Book 6 now gives a complete, usable Book 7 handoff. The party at the shelf is five; the shelf is the **second** camp past the Registry Line and the **first fire** past it; Cael has nine confirmed fragments plus one uncounted anomaly; Anchor is idle and undeployed; Shadow is sealed and undeployed since the Line; the four enrolled travelers resigned in good standing, while Seln filed nothing; and the file status is exactly *Status: active non-compliance, observation priority escalated.* (B6 ch55:7-11, 91-103, 167-187; ch57:15-19, 43-53, 111-117; ch59:235-305, 351-359; ch60:3-57, 195-229, 289-321; B6 ledger:1324-1332).
+
+The Book 7 plan is not ready as written. Its M1-blocking defects are amendable without a new owner ruling. After the ordered non-owner amendment list below is applied, **Movement 1 may be released for drafting**. Two protected-text questions remain owner items, but they first affect M4/M6-M8, not M1.
+
+### Citation convention
+
+`B6 chN:x-y` means the edition manuscript at `book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-N.md`, lines x-y. `B6 ledger:x-y` means the edition Book 6 `STATE_LEDGER.md`. Book 7 target citations name their file and present line. Every canon conclusion below carries an edition chapter:line; coordinator-only normalization is additionally cited to the binding ledger.
+
+---
+
+## F1 — closed Movement 8, chapters 48-54
+
+### F1.1 Ruling text and date
+
+The ruling is on **day 201, the last Fifth-day**, at the hour after noon. Its exact operative paragraph is:
+
+> *The seat, having heard the petition and the responses in full, and having found the enrollment lawful in its execution and the respondent institution compliant with its charter throughout — which findings stand undisturbed — nonetheless finds the evaluation-integrity question sustained on the merits. The demonstration provision describes the practitioner; it does not evaluate him within the meaning of the integrity provisions. The petition for compelled re-evaluation under standard Arbiter protocol is granted. The re-evaluation shall be conducted at the district Arbiter station within five weeks. Should the re-evaluation return no valid classification, the procedure of the code's chapter fourteen shall apply: nullification, suspension, asset-restriction. The demonstration-provision enrollment is revoked effective at the close of the present academic year.*
+>
+> *Given under the Compact's hand.*
+
+The text is B6 ch51:173-185. The preceding reservation sets the ruling for the last Fifth-day at the hour after noon (B6 ch49:217-219), and the ratified day number is 201 (B6 ledger:1168-1171).
+
+### F1.2 Brom
+
+Brom's panel reads him **Iron** and the district finds for advancement, but entry of that rank requires his signature within fourteen days (B6 ch51:127-155; ch52:131-145). He neither signs nor refuses the finding in M8; he sets the finding down unsigned beside the still-sealed Velmere envelope (B6 ch52:153-169; ch53:117-121). His formal standing at M8 close is therefore still **Copper**, specifically the continental Copper champion; M9 later closes the point as “Copper on that side ... for good,” because he never signs (B6 ch55:39-59; ch59:249-263). The Velmere letter remains sealed; the M9 coordinator places it in Hesk's satchel at the Book 7 handoff despite visible ch56 prose leaving it on Brom's table (B6 ch56:147-161; B6 ledger:1327, 1330).
+
+### F1.3 Lira
+
+M8 produces no Silver finding because Lira does not sit the scheduled evaluation. She prices the ladder, expressly retains **Iron Rank One**, and decides to leave it (B6 ch52:189-209). M9 makes the declined evaluation explicit: “I'm going east with them ... and I won't sit the Silver” (B6 ch56:53-75). Book 7 may therefore say: **Wind; Iron Rank One retained; Silver evaluation declined at full price** (B6 ch55:17-37; ch56:61-75).
+
+### F1.4 Karis
+
+Karis is the house's **advocate of record**: the seat grants the advocate leave, the clerk calls her in that capacity, and Jent later addresses her as “Advocate” (B6 ch48:75-87; ch49:43-59; ch51:213-215). At M8 close she has priced eight heads for forfeiture but has not yet lapsed them: annex, archive privileges, assistant allocation/letter, budget, Greyvane answer routing, research standing, and restricted-collection entry; her Ember Iron Rank Three is expressly retained (B6 ch52:211-235). The actual lapses occur at Bracken's counter in M9, while tier remains hers (B6 ch55:107-163).
+
+### F1.5 Blade notice and ninth fragment
+
+The exact notice is:
+
+```text
+FRAGMENT ACQUIRED
+[unnamed] — Blade-adjacent. Duration: sustained. Integration: partial.
+Tier equivalent: Iron.
+Note: edge-declaration component; line-reading component.
+Contact range.
+Acquisition: directed. Engagement: adversarial, earnest — non-hostile.
+```
+
+It appears at B6 ch54:145-152. The prose immediately counts **Nine** (B6 ch54:154). The acquisition is directed, adversarial, earnest, non-hostile, Iron-equivalent, contact-range, and only partially integrated; its components are edge-declaration and line-reading (B6 ch54:145-162). Its priced and realized costs are the left forearm, hip, shoulder, two ten-count Storm lanes, the behind-the-eyes bill, one spark, Ephram's unpriced shoulder, and the permanent cost of not telling Ephram what he gave (B6 ch53:101-115; ch54:97-137, 262-278). Blade is not deployed in the bout: Cael sees its proposed line and puts it down; the first integration pull comes later at the yard-gate lintel and is named quiet (B6 ch54:39-49, 282-292).
+
+### F1.6 Havel, Ilsev, Ephram
+
+Havel stops at **six sheets** and deliberately creates no seventh because the return is already public record (B6 ch51:81-95). Ilsev learns only the two registry returns, enters *Authorizing office: not traced*, notes the contradiction, makes no finding outside her scope, and learns neither cache nor integration mechanism (B6 ch50:235-263). Ephram learns that five people are leaving east past the Line and that Cael deliberately held back in their prior bouts; he does not learn the cache, the integration mechanism, or that he supplied Blade (B6 ch52:279-317; ch54:240-250, 262-266). The M8 knowledge wall therefore holds (B6 ledger:1187-1195).
+
+### F1.7 Gault and Vastin
+
+Gault remains the **evaluator of record**: the petitioner stipulates his competence, the proceeding identifies him in that office, and the narration distinguishes him from the certifying office (B6 ch48:45; ch49:199-209). Vastin remains **Archmarshal / the certifying office**; his office's certificate is the one declined, and he later returns the closed summary without annotation (B6 ch49:199-213; ch58:59-107). Book 7 must never relabel Vastin evaluator of record (B6 ledger:1161-1162, 1327).
