+## New findings created by closed M8-M9
+
+### N1 — shelf chronology
+
+The Book 7 map calls the shelf the first camp; closed prose makes the wet cart-canvas night the first camp past the Line and the shelf the second camp and first fire (B6 ch59:351-361; ch60:3-57). OWNER #46 already directs Book 7, so this is an amendment, not an owner item.
+
+### N2 — the road bill is ten-count, not eleven-minute
+
+`BOOK_MAP.md:19` says “eleven-minute bill.” The closed bout uses two ten-count lanes, and the road bill is the delayed headache/inability to eat from that work (B6 ch54:77-95, 113-137, 262-278; ch58:113-129, 281-303). Replace it with “ten-count bill.”
+
+### N3 — Velmere custody is missing from Book 7
+
+The M9 coordinator carries the still-sealed Velmere letter in Hesk's satchel, although visible ch56 leaves it on Brom's table (B6 ch56:147-161; B6 ledger:1330, 1346). Book 7 currently inventories neither that letter nor the full old volume. Both must be added to the satchel state.
+
+### N4 — two map records
+
+Book 7 inventories the printed sheet but does not preserve the separate entry markings. Karis's printed sheet and Lira's route book contain different, exact records (B6 ch60:135-167). Both must enter the state ledger.
+
+### N5 — Gault's last note is not a carried object
+
+`MOVEMENT-006.md:25` places Pike's delivered Fallow copy “beside Gault's last note.” Gault's note was entered at Bracken's counter with the withdrawal file; the party read it but did not carry the leaf east (B6 ch55:181-199). M6 may invoke Cael's memory of its last sentence, not stage the physical note.
+
+### N6 — cache knowledge and mechanism knowledge are distinct
+
+The Book 7 ledger states who knows the mechanism but omits the wider cache/falsification circle. At the handoff, six know the cache (the five travelers plus Vastin), while only the five travelers know the integration mechanism; Ephram and the academy do not (B6 ch52:61-105, 279-317; ch60:221-225; B6 ledger:1189-1194, 1348).
+
+### N7 — C1 is already owner-ruled
+
+The cart/gelding do exist at the seam, the purse survives, and OWNER #23 already orders their Lowmarch sale/reserve. `STATE_LEDGER.md:119` and `BOOK_MAP.md:350,379` still call that ruling pending (B6 ch56:169-197; ch60:173-187; OWNER #23). Remove the pending language.
+
