+### OI-1 — protected Quiet/Kindling language
+
+Protected lines `BOOK_MAP.md:279-282, 287, 312, 321` say variants of “mine didn't,” “my Path,” “mine has been asleep since I was fourteen,” “dark since fourteen,” and “every Path ... his had not.” Canon is: Cael's own Arbiter woke at Kindling, the station plate lit eleven seconds late, the failed-safe word replaced the old name, the Arbiter then went dark; at Quiet lines the dark Arbiter is unchanged while his fragments continue to answer (B6 ch50:269-273; ch59:265-305; earlier exact mechanism B6 ch36:117, ch37:15, ch39:59-63, 127-129).
+
+Options:
+
+1. Release only the minimum conflicting clauses for canon repair: five live Arbiters stop; Cael's was dark before and after; his fragments still answer.
+2. Release the full affected log entries for clean recomposition around Arbiter/plate/fragments.
+3. Keep the protected words as Cael's knowingly imprecise shorthand, but add an adjacent corrective log sentence each time. This is least clean and not recommended.
+
+This must be settled before M4 is drafted; the final close must be settled before M8.
+
+### OI-2 — protected “Six years I've wanted a face”
+
+`BOOK_MAP.md:314` protects “Six years I've wanted a face,” and `MOVEMENT-007.md:25` repeats it as protected. Closed canon says Seln has carried the case twelve years; no distinct six-year trigger for wanting a face is established (B6 ch57:133-145).
+
+Options:
+
+1. Change the protected line to “Twelve years I've wanted a face.”
+2. Remove the numeral: “All these years I've wanted a face.”
+3. Retain six only if the owner supplies a distinct event six years earlier that began the wish; the M7 plan must then name that trigger and keep it separate from the twelve-year case history.
+
+This need not delay M1; it must be resolved before M7.
