+## F2 — closed Movement 9, chapters 55-60
+
+### F2.1 People, withdrawals, departure form, Ephram, standings
+
+The final travelers are **Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln**. Ephram stays at Halcenvane with his right shoulder set and expected to remain in a sling for a month (B6 ch54:109-137, 232-250; ch56:229-253). Four enrolled travelers file withdrawals at Bracken's counter: Lira, Brom, Cael and Karis; Bracken enters each as *Withdrawn. Resigned in good standing* (B6 ch55:7-11, 13-59, 65-103, 107-167). Seln is staff, not an enrollee; he files no departure paper, leaves four keys and no note, exits off the gate's books, and later says, “I have filed nothing today” (B6 ch57:15-25, 43-53, 93-117; ch58:265-275).
+
+Exact entry standings are:
+
+- Cael: resigned in good standing, unclassified (B6 ch55:69-103).
+- Lira: Wind; Iron Rank One retained; Silver evaluation not sat (B6 ch55:17-37; ch56:53-75).
+- Brom: Iron Skin; formal Copper for good; continental Copper champion; Iron finding unsigned (B6 ch55:39-59; ch58:33-35; ch59:249-263).
+- Karis: Ember; Iron Rank Three retained; research standing, budget/allocation, annex, archive privileges and restricted-collection access lapsed (B6 ch55:107-163).
+- Seln: Shadow; Bronze; fifteen years' service; left without notice or form, not “in form” (B6 ch57:43-53, 59-87, 93-117).
+
+### F2.2 Calendar reconstruction
+
+The calendar is now proved:
+
+1. **Day 203, Seventh-day:** the morning after the day-202 bout, the four withdrawal leaves are signed; the four enrollees leave the hill at dusk (B6 ch55:3-11, 257-263; ch56:307-341; B6 ledger:1325).
+2. **Day 204, First-day:** the four leave Ostrand at first light; the desk clerk finds Seln's keys that morning; Seln meets them at the eighteenth-stone crossroads that dusk, making five (B6 ch57:3-17, 43-55, 177-227; ch58:113-131, 205-277).
+3. **Days 205-206:** second road day and hill/last-waystation day (B6 ch58:281-303; ch59:3-55).
+4. **Day 207, Fourth-day:** the academic year's last day occurs while they are still west of the Line; the watcher turns back at the provincial bound and the party reaches the last station (B6 ch59:105-149, 155-231).
+5. **Day 208:** they leave the station, cross the Registry Line before noon, and make the wet first camp past it under cart canvas with no fire (B6 ch59:235-305, 351-361).
+6. **Day 209, Sixth-day by the hill's count / second day past the Line by theirs:** they make the shelf camp and light the first fire past the Line (B6 ch60:3-57, 197-203).
+
+Thus Book 6's sixth day from Ostrand is Book 7's second day past the Line, counting the First-day departure as the first travel day (B6 ch58:113-131; ch60:197-203).
+
+### F2.3 Bodies and object ledger
+
+Cael enters Book 7 with no open injury. His five Blade bars have blurred into a brown-violet left-forearm bruise, one week old and one week from gone; the **ten-count** road bill of headache/inability to eat has already cleared (B6 ch58:113-129, 281-303; ch60:191-201; B6 ledger:1332). Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln have no open injury at the shelf; Ephram's shoulder remains behind at Halcenvane (B6 ch54:109-137, 232-250; ch60:103-113; B6 ledger:1342).
+
+The physical handoff is:
+
+- Hesk's satchel: the current log, about one-third blank leaves remaining; the full old volume; the observation notebook; the held Hesk and Vell letters; and, by binding coordinator ruling, the **sealed Velmere letter** (B6 ch59:369-381; ch60:191-195, 233-243, 277-285; B6 ledger:1330, 1346). The visible prose had left the sealed Velmere envelope on Brom's table, so this custody is a coordinator repair, not an inference from ch56 (B6 ch56:147-161; B6 ledger:1330).
+- Karis's three numbered boxes under the cart canvas. The middle box contains the registry's printed continental sheet and the Ternhall brass straightedge; the boxes also hold her field archive and masonry material (B6 ch56:185-245; ch58:125; ch60:117-163).
+- Seln's locked case, in/with his post satchel and under the canvas when the load is camped; it has been carried for twelve years and remains unopened on the road (B6 ch52:9-13; ch57:115, 133-145; ch60:221-225).
+- A two-wheeled cart and brown gelding with one white foot (B6 ch56:169-197; ch58:125-131; ch60:3-33).
+- The pooled purse after buying the cart, gelding and four nights' hay; the prose intentionally states no numeric total, only that it is larger than expected (B6 ch60:173-187).
+- Daeva's reply has gone west, without a return address (B6 ch59:369-381, 417-437). Hesk's and Vell's letters are written at the shelf, have no return address, and remain held for a later westbound carrier (B6 ch60:277-285).
+
+The map state is two records, not one: Karis marks the registry sheet *ridge* and *Shelf; a pine; water at 36*; Lira separately writes in her route book *Ridge: one horse, three boxes by hand. Scree: by hand again. Shelf.* (B6 ch60:135-167; B6 ledger:1331).
